public String sortString(String s) {
    if (s == null || s.isEmpty()) {
        return s;
    }
    char[] chars = s.toCharArray();
    Arrays.sort(chars);
    StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();
    while (result.length() < chars.length) {
        int minIndex = 0;
        int maxIndex = chars.length - 1;
        while (minIndex < maxIndex) {
            result.append(chars[minIndex]);
            minIndex++;
        }
        while (maxIndex >= 0) {
            result.append(chars[maxIndex]);
            maxIndex--;
        }
    }
    return result.toString();
}
```
This method first sorts the input string using the `Arrays.sort()` method. Then, it iterates over the sorted array of characters, appending the smallest character to the result string, then the second smallest, and so on, until all characters have been appended. Finally, it iterates over the sorted array in reverse order, appending the largest character to the result string, then the second largest, and so on, until all characters have been appended. The resulting string is returned.

Note that this method assumes that the input string is not null or empty. If the input string is null or empty, the method returns the input string as is.

