The method then initializes a variable `leftSum` to 0 and iterates over the elements in the array. For each element, it adds the element to `leftSum` and checks if `leftSum` is equal to `average`. If it is, the method returns `true`.

If the method completes the iteration without finding a match, it returns `false`.

public int minCostClimbingStairs(int[] cost) {
    int n = cost.length;
    int[] dp = new int[n];
    dp[0] = cost[0];
    dp[1] = cost[1];
    for (int i = 2; i < n; i++) {
        dp[i] = Math.min(dp[i - 1], dp[i - 2]) + cost[i];
    }
    return Math.min(dp[n - 1], dp[n - 2]);
}

public int uniqueMorseRepresentations(String[] words) {
    String[] morseCodes = {".-", "-...", "-.-.", "-..", ".", "..-.", "--.", "....", "..", ".---", "-.-", ".-..", "--", "-.", "---", ".--.", "--.-", ".-.", "...", "-", "..-", "...-", ".--", "-..-", "-.--", "--.."};
    Set<String> seen = new HashSet<>();
    for (String word : words) {
        StringBuilder code = new StringBuilder();
        for (char c : word.toCharArray()) {
            code.append(morseCodes[c - 'a']);
        }
        seen.add(code.toString());
    }
    return seen.size();
}

